  "name": "Jagar (Garhwal and Kumaon possession ritual song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Jagar ('awakening') is the night ritual of Garhwal and Kumaon in which a lead singer (jagariya) sings the stories of local gods and ancestral spirits to call them into the bodies of mediums, who begin to dance as the drumming intensifies. The songs are accompanied by the hudka hourglass drum or by the dhol and the small kettledrum damau played by hereditary drummers; the dhol card stands in for the Garhwali dhol and the nagara card for the damau.",
